  "homeActivities": [
    {
      "text": "Activity 1 — Sound boxes\nTake three small empty boxes or plastic containers. Put rice in the first, a stone or a coin in the second, cotton wool or a feather in the\nthird. Close them and shake each one. Ask: \"Which is loud? Which is quiet? Why do you think?\" Hard, heavy things make loud sounds.\nSoft, light things make almost none.\nActivity 2 — How far can you hear it?\nStand in one place and bang a pot with a wooden spoon. He walks away one step at a time, counting his steps, until he cannot hear it any\nmore. Write the number down. Now bang the pot harder and repeat. He can walk further this time.\nTwo lessons in one game: a louder sound travels further, and every sound gets fainter with distance.\ndrum 20 steps away\nloud quieter fainter and fainter\nThe further the sound travels, the fainter it gets — until the ear cannot catch it.\n",
      "safety": "An adult stays with the child for every activity. No glass, no sockets, no flames, and nothing small enough to swallow is left with a child\nalone. Water activities are done in a bowl or the sink, never near electrical items.",
      "pages": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "safetyPages": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
